<section id="problem">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">The coordination problem</p>
        <h2>Most stores don't have a technology shortage. They have a technology coordination problem.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">Your CRM works. Your DMS works. Your website, phones, inventory tool and service scheduler all work. The failures happen in the space between them — and nobody owns that space.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="story">
      <ol>
        <li><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">A customer submits a lead at 9:40 on a Saturday night.</span></li>
        <li><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">The CRM receives it and creates a task.</span></li>
        <li class="fail"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Nobody responds quickly.</span></li>
        <li><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">The BDC calls Monday afternoon.</span></li>
        <li><span class="n">05</span><span class="t">The customer replies by text instead.</span></li>
        <li class="fail"><span class="n">06</span><span class="t">The salesperson never sees the text.</span></li>
        <li class="fail"><span class="n">07</span><span class="t">The appointment is never confirmed.</span></li>
        <li class="fail"><span class="n">08</span><span class="t">The CRM says one thing. The DMS says another.</span></li>
        <li class="fail"><span class="n">09</span><span class="t">Management finds out two weeks later.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <p class="verdict">Nobody failed.<span>The system failed to produce a coherent process.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

